WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.004
Data control is a common reason for local inference.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:09.642
Prompts and outputs can remain within an approved environment when the application, logs,

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:12.678
interfaces, and supporting tools are configured accordingly.

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:15.714
Local execution does not automatically prevent leakage.

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:20.051
Offline capability can support field work, isolated labs, unreliable connectivity,

00:00:20.051 --> 00:00:21.353
or continuity needs.

00:00:21.353 --> 00:00:23.521
The model, runtime, dependencies, documentation,

00:00:23.521 --> 00:00:30.461
and required reference data must already be available and maintained for offline use to be meaningful.

00:00:30.461 --> 00:00:34.798
Local systems support experimentation with model families, quantizations, prompts, adapters,

00:00:34.798 --> 00:00:35.665
and runtimes.

00:00:35.665 --> 00:00:41.738
Teams can inspect performance and behavior without every request becoming a metered external call,

00:00:41.738 --> 00:00:46.075
although hardware, electricity, engineering time, and maintenance still have cost.

00:00:46.075 --> 00:00:50.846
Customization may include retrieval over approved data, structured workflows, domain prompts,

00:00:50.846 --> 00:00:53.882
fine-tuned or adapted models, and local integrations.

00:00:53.882 --> 00:00:57.785
Each change creates evaluation, security, provenance, and lifecycle responsibilities.

00:00:57.785 --> 00:01:02.990
Hosted models may offer stronger capability, larger context, managed scaling, rapid updates,

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:04.725
and less infrastructure work.

00:01:04.725 --> 00:01:09.496
Local models may have lower quality on difficult tasks, limited concurrency,

00:01:09.496 --> 00:01:12.966
hardware constraints, and slower access to new capabilities.

00:01:12.966 --> 00:01:16.436
Choose local when its control, latency, offline, integration,

00:01:16.436 --> 00:01:19.472
or economic benefits match a real requirement.

00:01:19.472 --> 00:01:26.411
Do not choose it solely to avoid governance or because hardware ownership feels equivalent to privacy.

00:01:26.411 --> 00:01:28.580
Hybrid approaches are often practical.
